<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sizzo III of Schwarzburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1160">1160</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sizzo III of Schwarzburg was a Thuringian nobleman who first called himself count of Schwarzburg in 1123, after the castle on the Schwarza river in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringian-forest">Thuringian Forest</a>. He is regarded as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-schwarzburg">House of Schwarzburg</a>, whose branches ruled principalities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> until 1918.</p></div>
